  "architectureNotes": [
    "The canonical collection is mandatory and supports lookup, hierarchy traversal, release diff, semantic scope resolution, and basic ECL/subsumption queries.",
    "The term sidecar is configurable but default-on. Search, clinical note mapping, and benchmark retrieval require it for production-quality behavior.",
    "Release updates are streamed from JSON so large official files do not need to fit in memory.",
    "The provider-neutral terminology gateway is outside this storage pack and can route SNOMED here while routing other code systems to customer-managed FHIR terminology servers.",
    "Lexical retrieval is the baseline and requires only MongoDB. Vector retrieval, cross-encoder reranking, and LLM extraction are optional per-environment bindings; when absent, the response states which path actually ran instead of implying the richer one.",
    "LLM extraction returns mentions and their context only. It never returns a SNOMED CT code, and adjudication may only choose among candidates retrieval already returned.",
    "Complex FHIR ValueSet.compose import, complete ECL, and native ConceptMap authoring are not implied by the current capability set."
  ]
